import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Retro — spike Q2: what does the boundary cost?","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Retro — spike Q2: what does the boundary cost?","type":"retro","date":"2026-10-14T00:00:00.000Z"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/retros/handl-q2-boundary-cost.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/retros/handl-q2-boundary-cost.md"}`),a={name:`graphopt/project/retros/handl-q2-boundary-cost.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="retro-—-spike-q2-what-does-the-boundary-cost" tabindex="-1">Retro — spike Q2: what does the boundary cost? <a class="header-anchor" href="#retro-—-spike-q2-what-does-the-boundary-cost" aria-label="Permalink to “Retro — spike Q2: what does the boundary cost?”">​</a></h1><p><strong>Plan</strong>: 0029, <strong>Q2</strong>. <strong>Verdict</strong>: <strong>not applicable as posed</strong> — and the reason is a decision, not a dodge. The measured cost of the v1 path is the fragment load, which is negligible.</p><h2 id="the-question-as-the-plan-posed-it" tabindex="-1">The question, as the plan posed it <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-question-as-the-plan-posed-it" aria-label="Permalink to “The question, as the plan posed it”">​</a></h2><blockquote><p><strong>Pass criterion is <em>not</em> &quot;faster&quot;</strong> … the criterion is: host-fn dispatch must not dominate <strong>rewrite throughput</strong> — measure rewrites/second through handl&#39;s engine on a small law set and compare with catopt&#39;s e-graph on the same set. Pass = same order of magnitude; the exec timing is informational.</p></blockquote><h2 id="why-it-does-not-apply" tabindex="-1">Why it does not apply <a class="header-anchor" href="#why-it-does-not-apply" aria-label="Permalink to “Why it does not apply”">​</a></h2><p>The question assumes <strong>host functions in the path</strong> — that tensor ops cross the boundary during rewriting. Two measurements remove that assumption:</p><ol><li><strong>ADR 0011</strong> decides the integration is <strong>language-only in v1</strong>: rewriting is canonical in the calculus, execution stays catopt&#39;s, and no tensor needs to cross.</li><li><strong>Q1b</strong> shows that if a tensor <em>did</em> cross, it would cross as a raw process-local pointer through a debug encoding (<code>{&quot;__resource__&quot;: {&quot;ptr&quot;: n}}</code>) or as copied bytes — i.e. the expensive thing the question was trying to bound is exactly the thing the decision avoids.</li></ol><p>So there is no host-fn dispatch to measure in the v1 path. Measuring it would be measuring a design we chose not to build.</p><h2 id="what-is-measured" tabindex="-1">What <em>is</em> measured <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-is-measured" aria-label="Permalink to “What is measured”">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>stage</th><th>cost</th><th>source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>fragment load (<code>language_from_dir</code> over the ten-file dir)</td><td><strong>instant</strong> — the spike&#39;s test reports <code>finished in 0.00s</code> for the merge + both assertions</td><td>handl <code>b20b978a</code> (<code>catopt_fragments.rs</code>)</td></tr><tr><td>the rewrite pass itself</td><td>handl&#39;s own engine cost, already covered by handl&#39;s suite (4,288 tests); not catopt&#39;s to measure</td><td>handl</td></tr><tr><td>catopt&#39;s side of the seam</td><td>the emitter (<code>store_to_handl</code>) — pure dict construction, no I/O, no tensors</td><td>catopt <code>lab/handl-spike/dump_fragments.py</code></td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="the-honest-caveats" tabindex="-1">The honest caveats <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-honest-caveats" aria-label="Permalink to “The honest caveats”">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>&quot;Instant&quot; is a small fixture.</strong> One law + a handful of shapes. The <em>load</em> cost scales with the bank (82 rules, ~35 op shapes) — still trivial in absolute terms, but the claim should be re-measured on the full bank before it is quoted. (<code>dump_fragments.py --all</code> emits it; nobody has loaded the full bank yet.)</li><li><strong>Rewrite throughput was not compared</strong> — deliberately, per the above. If a future version routes tensor ops through the boundary, this retro must be redone with the original criterion, and the pointer route&#39;s cost (an integer in JSON per crossing, plus the host&#39;s lookup) is what would be measured.</li><li><strong>The exec timing is untouched.</strong> catopt&#39;s executors are unchanged and unmeasured here; the boundary does not sit in their path.</li></ul><h2 id="what-this-buys" tabindex="-1">What this buys <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-this-buys" aria-label="Permalink to “What this buys”">​</a></h2><p>It closes a question by <strong>decision + measurement</strong> rather than by benchmark: the boundary&#39;s v1 cost is the load, and the load is negligible. If the integration later grows a tensor channel, the original criterion is the one to apply — and it is written down.</p>`,14)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};